e of heavy supporting fire or diversionary attacks. There is a misconception that the Red Army relied mostly on frontal assaults or “human wave attack” tactics, but they did occur, same as in all armies fighting in WWII.","LocalizedString":"A frontal assault is a military tactic which is a direct movement of forces towards the front of an enemy position. Often this tactic is used as a last resort since the attackers are subjecting themselves to the maximum defensive power of the enemy. The risks can be minimized to some extent by the use of cover, such as smokescreen or darkness of night, and use of heavy supporting fire or diversionary attacks. There is a misconception that the Red Army relied mostly on frontal assaults or “human wave attack” tactics, but they did occur, same as in all armies fighting in WWII."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","spawnCardName":"card_unit_light_infantry","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'The_Hammer'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/The_Hammer.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/t_soviet_ordersky.t_soviet_ordersky","SubPathString":""},"artist":"SPUTNIK / Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FRONTAL_ASSAULT.FRONTAL_ASSAULT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":393.0},"historyPhotoSource":"RIA Novosti archive","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"613694","historyPhotoAuthor":"Ivan Shagin","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_assault_photo","SourceString":"Red Army soldiers on the offensive near Bryansk, 1943.","LocalizedString":"Red Army soldiers on the offensive near Bryansk, 1943."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"tempCard",